  "contradictory_evidence": [
    "Large-N independent evaluator-gated rare-hit search can help, while large-N tightly coupled free-form coordination can sharply reduce correctness.",
    "Structured coordination can recover coupled-task accuracy, but one-shot commitment regressed one Qwen3 P2P setting; no component is universal.",
    "More/full context or replay is non-monotonic; controlled pollution reveals retention differences hidden on clean saturated workloads, and random replay can increase forgetting in scoped settings.",
    "Monitor predictive accuracy is not intervention utility: AUROC 0.94 coexisted with up to -26 percentage-point downstream impact, while intervention helped a high-failure regime.",
    "Many local errors repair; every observed error is not terminal negative evidence.",
    "Persistence availability is not behavioral use: matched on/off and pathway telemetry show routing/consult/update failures and non-monotonic component interactions.",
    "Cross-lineage/archive diversity can improve search, but unrestricted sharing can propagate weak or obsolete evidence and component causality is often bundled.",
    "Evaluator/judge agreement is not endpoint validity; dense diagnostic rubrics can agree strongly while correlating weakly with deterministic success.",
